// Mystery: original stories written for this game. Format: docs/v3/BLUEPRINT-FORMAT.md.

== mystery.f01 | feature | chapters
title: The Missing Chapter
genre: mystery + costume-drama
tone: Lacquered, hushed and sly
era: 1010 | period
setting: The Empress's apartments, Heian-kyo | real | institution
logline: When the newest chapter of the court's favourite tale vanishes the night before it is to be read to the Emperor, a junior lady-in-waiting has until dusk to find it among women who communicate entirely in poems.
premise: A tale is being written a chapter at a time by a lady of the Empress's household, and the whole court waits for it. The fair copy of the newest chapter has gone from its box. Nobody may be accused; nobody may even be asked directly. {shonagon_no}, called the Minor Counsellor's girl, is too junior to matter and so may go anywhere.
synopsis: The chapter was to be read at the hour of the cock. At dawn the box holds blank paper of the right weight. Its author, {murasaki}, says only that it is a pity, and begins grinding ink. The Empress's senior lady, {saisho}, gives the junior girl the errand of finding it without anyone noticing it is lost. The film proceeds by rooms and by poems: every question must be put as an allusion, and every answer comes back folded on coloured paper tied to a branch. A rival salon would pay for the chapter; a jilted captain of the guard appears in it thinly disguised; a copyist has been promised a place and not given it. {shonagon_no} learns to read what the paper says apart from the words: the grade, the scent, the knot. The blank sheets in the box are from the author's own stock. The thief is {murasaki} herself. The chapter kills its hero, the court will not forgive her for it, and the Regent has let her know that a tale which pleases is a household's ornament and a tale which grieves is a liability. She has not destroyed it; a writer cannot. It is sewn into the lining of the girl's own robe, the one place nobody searches. {shonagon_no} must choose between returning it, which exposes the author, and staying silent, which loses it. She reads the chapter at dusk herself, from memory, as if it were gossip, in the wrong order, to the Empress alone. The Empress weeps and asks for it to be copied. The author looks at the girl for a long moment and hands her a brush.
question: Who owns a story once people are waiting for it?
themes: authorship under patronage; indirection as a language; the courage to disappoint
audience: Adults who like puzzles and manners
viewpoint: With {shonagon_no}, who sees everything from behind screens
stakes: A chapter, an author's place at court, and a girl's first and only errand of consequence
conflict: A junior lady's need to succeed against the discovery that success would ruin the person she most admires
ending: The chapter is delivered as hearsay and loved. The author keeps her place and takes an apprentice.
experience: The pleasure of decoding, a twist that is also a kindness, and the hush of a room hearing something sad
look: Twelve-layered sleeves under blinds, lamplight on gold dust paper; faces half seen through screens
sound: Silk, rain on cypress bark, an inkstone. A koto tuned and never played until the reading.
m: find | secret | loyalty-vs-truth | reconciled
@ shonagon_no | The Minor Counsellor's Girl | lead | protagonist | human | she/her | 17 | To do one thing well enough to be given a name | She is known only by her father's rank | Nobody may be asked a direct question | Observant, literal, learning not to be | From errand girl to reader to apprentice | Too plain at first; then in borrowed verse | Sleeves in the wrong season's colours
@ murasaki | The Lady Of The Tale | co-lead | antagonist | human | she/her | 37 | To have written the chapter as it had to be | Her hero must die for the tale to be true | The Regent wants a pleasant book | Reserved, exact, unrepentant | From hiding the chapter to handing on the brush | Almost silent; devastating in verse | Dark robes, ink on the heel of her hand
@ saisho | Lady Saisho | supporting | mentor | human | she/her | 45 | The household unembarrassed by dusk | She has kept this salon above its rival for ten years | She cannot be seen to look | Smooth, worldly, kinder than she appears | From commanding the search to covering for its result | Lightly mocking, perfectly allusive | Faultless layers, a fan she speaks through
@ korechika | Captain Korechika | featured | foil | human | he/him | 30 | To know what the tale says of him | He courted the author and was written down for it | He is vain enough to be recognised | Handsome, sulky, transparent | From suspect to a man who would rather be mocked than left out | Loud for the setting; bad verses | Hunting costume, a branch of blossom slightly past its day
~ shonagon_no - murasaki | junior lady and the author she admires | awe | a brush handed across
~ shonagon_no - saisho | errand girl and senior lady | an order | a look that says she knows and approves
~ murasaki - korechika | author and model | a courtship she ended | a character she killed
# The Box | INT | Empress's Apartments, Writing Alcove | DAWN | shonagon_no, murasaki, saisho | Open it | The box holds blank paper. {murasaki} says it is a pity and begins to grind ink. {saisho} gives the girl until dusk | The chapter is missing | 4 | props=lacquer box+blank paper+inkstone
# The Poems | INT | Western Gallery | DAY | shonagon_no, korechika | Question a suspect | She sends him a verse about fallen blossom. He answers in person, loudly, wanting to know what the tale says of him | | 5 | props=poem slips+blossom branch
# The Poems | INT | Copyists' Room | DAY | shonagon_no, saisho | Read the paper | Not the words: the weight, the scent, the knot. The blank sheets in the box are from one person's stock | {shonagon_no} knows whose paper it is | 5 | props=paper stock+scent box
# The Lining | INT | Shonagon's Sleeping Space | DUSK | shonagon_no, murasaki | Find it | Her own robe hangs oddly. The chapter is sewn into its lining. {murasaki}, behind the screen, does not deny it | The author is the thief | 6 | props=robe+hidden manuscript
# The Reading | INT | Empress's Presence Chamber | NIGHT | shonagon_no, saisho, murasaki, korechika | Tell it as gossip | She gives the chapter from memory, out of order, as something she heard. The koto is finally played. Behind a curtain someone weeps | The chapter is heard | 7 | crowd=20, props=koto
# The Reading | INT | Writing Alcove | NIGHT | shonagon_no, murasaki | Be given a brush | A fresh sheet between them. {murasaki} wets the brush and holds it out | | 3 | props=brush+paper
review: authored | 2026-11-12 | written whole; drawn from the women's salons of the Heian court, with invented people
